processes, at most \code{n_resamples} of them, and each worker's random forest
gets the core count divided by the number of workers. With \code{n_jobs = 1}
one process runs every resample and the forest uses every core; with
\code{n_jobs = -1} there is one worker per core, each with a single-threaded
forest. Every worker holds its own copy of the data and of its forest, so
